      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'd prefer world creators to have the ability to stop players from seeing other players. You should always have the right to see yourself in the mirror. The mirror is a tool for some people.\n\nI'm always for giving world creators more control over how the map limits certain functions, because I have 0 doubt in my mind that good world creators will implement this correctly if they had this option. Best case scenario, it can be changed at runtime, allowing scriptable buttons to allow instance masters to enable or disable it at the instances discretion.",
